@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Applications";
    Layout = "_Layout"; 
}
<div class="d-flex justify-content-center gap-0 my-4">
<h2> Applications</h2>
</div>

<div class="d-flex justify-content-center gap-3 my-4">
<a asp-controller="CoachApplication" asp-action= "List" class="btn btn-primary">
    Coach
</a>

<a asp-controller="PlayerApplication" asp-action="List" class="btn btn-primary">
    Player
</a>
</div>

@* This code creates a simple web page for the "Applications" section of your app.
What it does:
•	Sets the page title to "Applications" and uses the shared layout (_Layout).
•	Displays a heading: "Applications".
•	Shows two buttons in the center of the page:
•	Coach: Takes the user to the list of coach applications.
•	Player: Takes the user to the list of player applications.
In short:
This page lets users choose to view either coach or player applications by clicking the appropriate button. *@